{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"6efcf585aed6cbe63cd5e04055789195b12ff6aa48ffe0aac74195e806700a49","digest":{"component_or_area":"code-review gate model configuration and resolution","key_entities":["code-review.yaml","REBAR_LLM_MODEL","model_classes.py","resolve_model_string","batch step model_ladder","frontier","standard","cfg.model","verify.py","completion.py","interpreter.py:384-395","runners.py:128-130"],"problem_keywords":["per-pass model configuration","model class resolution","provider-aware model selection","environment variable limitation","batch step model declaration"],"propositions":["The code-review gate's four steps (base, round_a, round_b, coach) implicitly inherit a single cfg.model instead of declaring per-pass model classes.","A single REBAR_LLM_MODEL environment variable cannot express the required four-pass model mapping: Pass-1 finder on opus-family, Pass-2/Pass-4 verifier on sonnet-family.","Step-level model declarations on batch steps are silently ignored because the batch path reads only the batch sub-dict's model_ladder, not the enclosing step's model key.","Per-pass model resolution on non-default providers (Bedrock) currently collapses to a single model because undeclared steps inherit cfg.model rather than resolving their declared class."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787360292814108001,"uuid":"150a9845-8897-4f3f-aefe-e86087b34ba0"}